      detail: "WPFW is unapologetically political on the air, and it receives hostile contact. Take it seriously and take it calmly \u2014 those two are not in tension.\n\nExact words matter more than your summary of them, so write them down rather than paraphrasing later.\n\nTell the General Manager the same day either way, even if it seemed like nothing. Patterns only become visible when every instance gets reported, and the one you shrug off is often the one that mattered.\n\nIf a threat arrives while you are on the air, finish your break normally. Do not react to it on the microphone.\n\nIf a bomb threat comes by phone: keep them talking, and do not hang up even after they do \u2014 leave the line open. Write their exact words, and note background sounds, accent, tone, and whether they seem to be reading. If you can, ask where it is, when it will go off, what it looks like, what will set it off, whether they placed it, why, and what their name is. Signal somebody to call 911 while you stay on the line.",
