      detail: "Three different categories, and they are not treated the same. Obscenity has no First Amendment protection and may not be broadcast at any hour. Indecent and profane material is legal but restricted to the safe harbor, 10pm to 6am, when children are less likely to be in the audience.\n\nThe practical rule for a live show: if you would not say it at a church supper, do not say it before 10pm. And remember your guests and your callers are your responsibility on your show, not theirs.",
