      detail: "The order matters. Correcting yourself at length on air, and especially restating what was said while apologizing for it, makes things worse rather than better.\n\nWrite down the approximate timestamp and what was said straight away, before the wording slips. By the time anyone asks, you will not remember it accurately.\n\nThen tell management the same day \u2014 Katea Stitt at kstitt@wpfw.org or Shayna at gm@wpfw.org. Management notifies Pacifica Compliance. You will not be punished for reporting.\n\nIf a caller turns abusive, threatening or obscene, drop the call. You do not owe a hostile caller airtime. Screen for conduct, never for political viewpoint. If they make a specific threat \u2014 a person, a place, a time \u2014 write it down word for word, call 911, then call the General Manager.",
