      detail: "The notice has to come at the beginning of the call. Someone who rings the station’s on-air line is generally understood to have consented by calling in. A call you place out is different — say plainly that you are recording for broadcast before you start.\n\nThis is a federal broadcast rule and it is separate from DC and Maryland and Virginia wiretap law, which also apply and are stricter in some of those states. When in doubt, say it out loud and get them to say yes on the tape.",
