      detail: "The notice is a federal rule, not a courtesy. Before you record a call for broadcast or put a live call on the air, the other party has to be told. Somebody who rings the station\u2019s line has consented by calling in; a call you place out has not.\n\nZoom is the station\u2019s main platform for remote hosts and guests. Your show\u2019s standing link lives in the WPFW Program Information and Rundown spreadsheet, and the operator opens the room before the hour.\n\nBe in the room by :56 of the previous hour. The operator is admitting people, checking audio and running the previous show all at once.\n\nWired headphones and a wired connection beat wifi and laptop speakers every time \u2014 laptop speakers are what listeners hear as echo.\n\nIf Zoom drops mid-show, call the studio line immediately on 202-588-0893. Do not spend four minutes trying to rejoin silently; the operator does not know whether you are coming back.",
