      a: "At least 24 hours before it airs. Send it as a file, never as a link.",
      detail: "Twenty-four hours is the minimum, not the target. It exists so that somebody can check the file actually plays while there is still time to do something about it.\n\nSend it as a file. Every rundown that arrives as a link costs the operator time they do not have, usually at the worst possible moment.\n\nYour intro and outro music lives in the AM or PM folder on the studio PC. If you change your theme, tell production \u2014 do not assume the operator will find a new file you swapped in without telling anybody. Play at least thirty to forty seconds of the intro and outro unless you have agreed otherwise with the operator that day.",
