  /* ============================================================
     GUESTS WORTH BOOKING
     ------------------------------------------------------------
     This file is the "who to consider" half of the Guests view.
     The other half — who has actually been on — lives on the
     Guests tab of the content spreadsheet, because it grows every
     week and staff need to add to it without touching code.
  
     To add somebody, copy a block and edit it. Fields:
  
       name   as you would say it on air
       what   what they are. "Tenant organizer", "Saxophonist"
       org    where they do it, or their outlet. Optional
       beat   one of the keys in WPFW_GUEST_BEATS below
       why    why they are worth an hour. Be concrete
       find   where to find them. PUBLIC professional presence
              only — never somebody's personal email or phone.
              Put a BARE DOMAIN in here and the page turns it into
              a link: deanspade.net, not https://deanspade.net and
              not "his website". Anything with no domain in it still
              gets a "look them up" search beside it, so a label
              like "Alligator Records" is fine — but a domain is
              better, and a domain you have actually opened is best.
              A dead link is worse than no link.
       caution optional. A legal or safety condition on booking
              this person, shown in a red box above everything
              else. Use it for anyone running for office, for a
              live court case, or for a guest who may need to be
              pre-recorded or identified carefully. It is the one
              field on this page that can protect the licence.
       dc     true for anyone in DC or the DMV, which puts a
              green flag on them. A local guest can come into the
              studio, and that is worth more than a famous name
              on a book tour
  
     Two rules that keep this list useful rather than embarrassing:
  
     1. Bias young. The station already books the same established
        names. If somebody has been doing the interview circuit for
        thirty years, they do not need this list.
     2. Do not put a political label on anyone that they do not use
        about themselves. Describe the work instead. "Organizes
        tenants in Ward 8" is a fact. Anything else is a guess.
     ============================================================ */
  
